<title>PHILIPPINES: MRC to buy back shares from market.</title>
<headline>MRC to buy back shares from market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estate developer MRC Allied Industries Inc  said on Friday its board had approved a buyback programme of its shares.</p>
<p>The company told the Philippine Stock Exchange the MRC board had authorised  its management &quot;to purchase its own shares of stock from the open  market under terms and conditions which management may determine to  be most advantageous to the corporation.&quot;</p>
<p>MRC did not allot a specific amount for the buyback, but said it would  implement the programme as long as there is sufficient retained earnings  to support such purchases.</p>
<p>No other details were available.</p>
<p>MRC, which closed at 2.65 pesos on Thursday, was still untraded.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
